      "id": 1,
      "text": "Neskowin is an unincorporated community in Tillamook County located along the Pacific Ocean between Cascade Head and Nestucca Bay.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neskowin%2C_Oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The beach in Neskowin stretches over three miles long, extending from the mouth of the Nestucca River to its southern tip.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://tillamookcoast.com/plan-your-trip/where-to-go/destination/neskowin/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Dramatic Cascade Head rises to 1,200 feet above the coastline near the village of Neskowin.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://tillamookcoast.com/plan-your-trip/where-to-go/destination/neskowin/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Neskowin evolved over a century from a simple campground and hotel into a village of cottages, homes, and a golf course.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
